1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,372
When hundreds of alarms fire together, the first cause gets buried.

2
00:00:04,781 --> 00:00:08,000
TripLens reconstructs the incident behind the noise.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:16,408
For process engineers, TripLens connects eighteen observed channels, two control loops, and a
branching process graph.

4
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:21,342
Twelve incident sessions put different fault hypotheses to the test.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,246
Here, cooling demand rises, but valve feedback stays low.

6
00:00:28,146 --> 00:00:30,891
Flow falls, and reactor temperature follows.

7
00:00:31,791 --> 00:00:35,738
Compare competing causes, including the evidence against each one.

8
00:00:36,638 --> 00:00:40,760
Rewind the investigation to see only what was known at that moment.

9
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,396
A second session tells a different story: a frozen pressure sensor.

10
00:00:49,296 --> 00:00:51,258
Independent channels keep moving.

11
00:00:52,158 --> 00:00:56,946
TripLens flags the bad measurement and excludes it from strong process evidence.

12
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:07,141
The cooling-valve incident produces three hundred twelve events, six unique conditions, and
three process groups.

13
00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:12,690
Activations, repeated annunciations, and returns remain inspectable.

14
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,666
Now ask what could still prevent the trip.

15
00:01:17,566 --> 00:01:24,725
TripLens fits the leading hypothesis, then computes seven interventions across fifteen hundred
forty-seven branches.

16
00:01:25,625 --> 00:01:30,955
For the cooling bypass, one hundred one seconds is the last safe start in this model window.

17
00:01:31,855 --> 00:01:34,414
One second later, pressure crosses the limit.

18
00:01:35,314 --> 00:01:40,961
Emergency cooling buys two more seconds. A backup pump cannot resolve this stuck valve.

19
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:48,129
Every investigation step exposes its inputs and calculated output.

20
00:01:48,908 --> 00:01:54,654
Controller behavior, competing hypotheses, and procedure preconditions remain visible.

21
00:01:55,434 --> 00:02:01,000
Export the full root-cause dossier, including uncertainty and counterfactual results.

22
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:05,287
Save the incident fingerprint and operator note.

23
00:02:06,056 --> 00:02:12,540
Retrieve similar sessions, review repeated alarms, and inspect thirty-six internal parameter
variants.

24
00:02:13,309 --> 00:02:18,370
These checks are simulator regressions, not independent industrial validation.

25
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:22,000
New signal windows can enter through CSV.

26
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:27,407
Native Python computes the evidence and verifies interventions.

27
00:02:27,707 --> 00:02:33,094
A structured interface is prepared for NVIDIA Nemotron through Nebius Token Factory.

28
00:02:33,394 --> 00:02:39,297
This recording uses the local investigation policy; live provider integration is pending.

29
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:45,169
From alarm floods to an investigation you can inspect, challenge, and replay.

30
00:02:45,629 --> 00:02:49,000
TripLens. Follow the evidence. Change the outcome.
